  "code": "2823",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Autoimmune reactivities are not by themselves diagnostic, but must be correlated&nbsp;with other laboratory &amp; clinical findings.</p>\n<p><strong>Comments</strong><br>Parietal cell antibodies (APCA) are found predominantly in patients with&nbsp;Pernicious anemia (90%) and Autoimmune gastritis Type A (Chronic atrophic&nbsp;gastritis - 50%). These antibodies have also been found in patients with<br>associated organ specific diseases like Insulin Dependent Diabetes mellitus,&nbsp;Hypothyroidism &amp; Addison&rsquo;s disease. 2-15% of healthy individuals may also show these&nbsp;antibodies in low titres.</p>",
